From f7cd8efaf29874ea4a9651ce7a9c26dc2a01b922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marouene Boubakri <marouene.boubakri@nxp.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 17:38:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] IIOTSOL1-1589: IsoMux: enable TLS 1.3 cipher suites for ISO
 15118-20

IsoMux's TLS server unconditionally disables TLS 1.3 via an empty
`ciphersuites` string and pins the legacy TLS 1.2 suite mandated by
ISO 15118-2 (`ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-SHA256`). The comment in build_config
states `// disable TLS 1.3` explicitly.

This breaks ISO 15118-20 entirely. The standard mandates TLS 1.3
(Annex B) and the EV's TLS stack typically advertises only TLS 1.3 in
its `supported_versions` extension. Two failure modes are observed:

  1. Strict EVs reject IsoMux's ServerHello immediately because no
     TLS 1.3 was offered.

  2. Permissive EVs negotiate TLS 1.2 with the ISO 15118-2 cipher,
     then fail signature verification on CertificateVerify with
     `decrypt_error` (alert 51), because the cipher implies ISO
     15118-2 profile but the V2G leaf cert provided by EvseSecurity
     may be P-521/SHA-512 (per ISO 15118-20 cert profile).

ISO 15118-20 standalone (Evse15118D20 without IsoMux) is unaffected,
since that module uses a different TLS stack (libiso15118) which is
correctly configured for TLS 1.3. The bug is specific to IsoMux's
TLS termination, which reuses the OpenSSL wrapper from EvseV2G.

Enable the two TLS 1.3 cipher suites mandated by ISO 15118-20 Annex B
(`TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256` and `TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256`) alongside
the existing TLS 1.2 cipher. Existing ISO 15118-2 deployments continue
to negotiate TLS 1.2 (clients pick the offered TLS 1.2 cipher);
ISO 15118-20 deployments can now negotiate TLS 1.3.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Marouene Boubakri <marouene.boubakri@nxp.com>
---
 modules/EVSE/IsoMux/connection/tls_connection.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/EVSE/IsoMux/connection/tls_connection.cpp b/modules/EVSE/IsoMux/connection/tls_connection.cpp
index 86ac8b5..4a44198 100644
--- a/modules/EVSE/IsoMux/connection/tls_connection.cpp
+++ b/modules/EVSE/IsoMux/connection/tls_connection.cpp
@@ -275,9 +275,16 @@ bool build_config(tls::Server::config_t& config, struct v2g_context* ctx) {
 
     bool bResult{false};
 
+    // TLS 1.2 cipher list mandated by ISO 15118-2 (Annex H) and
+    // TLS 1.3 ciphersuites mandated by ISO 15118-20 (Annex B). Both
+    // protocol families terminate TLS here; the EV's ClientHello
+    // selects which version is negotiated.
     config.cipher_list = "ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-SHA256";
-    config.ciphersuites = "";     // disable TLS 1.3
-    config.verify_client = false; // contract certificate managed in-band in 15118-2
+    config.ciphersuites = "TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256:TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256";
+
+    // ISO 15118-2 manages contract certificates in-band, not via TLS
+    // client auth. ISO 15118-20 also does not use TLS client auth.
+    config.verify_client = false;
 
     // use the existing configured socket
     // TODO(james-ctc): switch to server socket init code otherwise there
-- 
